{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And Laban had two daughters, etc.</b> The verse intends to say that they were recognized and well-known, that the elder was Leah and the younger was Rachel, so that he could not say that the elder was the one called Rachel. Also, he was precise to say ״the elder״ ״the younger״ to say that they were not in a category of being exchangeable, so that he could make the younger into the elder and deceive Jacob by giving him Leah and saying that she is the younger whose name is Rachel — for the elder was greatly older and the younger greatly younger. And His saying <b>the elder</b> means that Leah was elder in her own right, not merely relative to Rachel was she older than her by a year or two, where the distinction would not be so clear; and Rachel likewise was greatly younger in her own right, not merely relative to Leah alone — as you may say, for Leah was twenty years old or above and Rachel was about five or seven, and from this there was no room for Laban to deceive Jacob with his conditions."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:44:42.021526551Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}